{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לא תתן מכשל", :translit "lo titen mikhshol", :gloss "you shall not place a stumbling block"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "לא תתן מכשל spelled deficient (without vav) — so even verbal advice counts, not just a literal obstacle."}], :frame {:text "The phrase לפני עור לא תתן מכשל at Leviticus 19:14 is read broadly: the Talmud derives that one must not give harmful advice to another, extending beyond a literal obstacle (Pesachim 22b). Rashi on Leviticus 19:14 glosses this as 'do not give advice that is improper for him.' The Ba'al HaTurim compresses this into the orthographic observation that the defective spelling supports the extended reading.", :sources ["Leviticus 19:14" "Pesachim 22b" "Rashi on Leviticus 19:14"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ויראת מאלהיך", :translit "v'yareita me'elokecha", :gloss "and fear your God"} {:he "לא תעשו עול במשפט", :translit "lo ta'asu ol ba'mishpat", :gloss "you shall do no injustice in judgment"} {:he "כי לא לאדם תשפטו כי אם לה'", :translit "ki lo la'adam tishpotu ki im la'shem", :gloss "for you do not judge for man but for Hashem"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contextual adjacency: ויראת מאלהיך (Lev 19:14) is immediately followed by לא תעשו עול במשפט (Lev 19:35)."}], :frame {:text "The verse ויראת מאלהיך at Leviticus 19:14 is immediately followed by לא תעשו עול במשפט at Leviticus 19:35. The statement כי לא לאדם תשפטו כי אם לה' paraphrases II Chronicles 19:6, where Jehoshaphat tells judges: 'for you do not judge for man but for the LORD.' The Talmud at Shabbat 10a states that every judge who judges truthfully is considered a partner with the Holy One.", :sources ["Leviticus 19:14" "Leviticus 19:35" "II Chronicles 19:6" "Shabbat 10a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "לא תתן מכשל spelled deficient (without vav) — so even verbal advice counts, not just a literal obstacle.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Contextual adjacency: ויראת מאלהיך (Lev 19:14) is immediately followed by לא תעשו עול במשפט (Lev 19:35).", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:24:18.004954654Z", :model "glm-5.2"}